        "original_id": "e4532763-71ee-5517-abf2-ac0d605012a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Juan Carlos Onetti, Richard Llewellyn, Stanley Baker\n- Works: Para esta noche, Nuit de chien, How Green Was My Valley\n- Organizations: BBC Television\n- Places: Montevideo, Madrid\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Llewellyn, born Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd, was born on 8 December 1906 and died on 30 November 1983.\n- Juan Carlos Onetti Borges was born on July 1, 1909 in Montevideo and died on May 30, 1994 in Madrid.\n- Richard Llewellyn was a British novelist and wrote the novel How Green Was My Valley.\n- Juan Carlos Onetti was an Uruguayan novelist and author of short stories.\n- Nuit de chien is based on the novel Para esta noche by Juan Carlos Onetti.\n- How Green Was My Valley is a BBC Television serial based on the novel by Richard Llewellyn.\n- How Green Was My Valley features one of the last performances by Stanley Baker.",
